# On-stage demo script, in talk order. Full list of endpoints: examples.http
# The flood results are JSON: read out "succeeded", "failed" and "durationMs".

### 1. Blocking: one coffee (~3 s) on an executor-thread that waits the whole time
GET http://localhost:8080/beverage/blocking

### 2. Blocking flood: 50 threads + 25 queued, so 75 succeed, 25 fail, ~6 s
GET http://localhost:8080/beverage/blocking/flood?count=100

### 3. Reactive sequential: show the nested flatMap chain (~9 s)
GET http://localhost:8080/beverage/reactive/sequential

### 4. Reactive parallel: Uni.join(), three coffees in ~3 s on the event loop
GET http://localhost:8080/beverage/reactive/parallel

### 5. Virtual parallel: same code as blocking, three coffees in ~3 s on virtual threads
GET http://localhost:8080/beverage/virtual/parallel

### 6. Virtual flood: one virtual thread per task, all 100 succeed in ~3 s
GET http://localhost:8080/beverage/virtual/flood?count=100

### 7. Structured race (custom Joiner): bartender-N threads, one "Served", the others "Cancelled after N ms", then "Scope closed"
GET http://localhost:8080/beverage/structured/race/custom
